<title>NETHERLANDS: Van Ommeren, Preussag TO merge container units.</title>
<headline>Van Ommeren, Preussag TO merge container units.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipping and tank storage firm Koninklijke van Ommeren NV said on Thursday it and Preussag AG's Vereinigte Tanklager und Transportmittel GmbH (VTG) would merge their container activities.</p>
<p>Van Ommeren will take a 40 percent stake in VTG's Hamburg-based tank container subsidiary, which will be renamed VOTG Tanktainer GmbH. Leasing activities will be combined in Peacock Tankcontainerleasing AG, which will be a 50-50 joint venture.</p>
<p>The new VOTG combine will have annual turnover of about 140 million guilders, Van Ommeren said.</p>
